{
  "version": "dexscreener-v5",
  "namespace": "dexscreener",
  "description": "Retrieval-verification dataset for the dexscreener namespace. Every live tool carries at least one blind row (outcome phrased without naming the brand) and at least one protocol-aware row (the brand is named), with the exact full toolId as the expectation. v2 (stage S2b) added the eight site-screening tools: the six leaderboard boards, the chain catalog and the token-level screen. v3 (stage S3) added the three resolve and market-context tools that stage could land: the single-pair live snapshot, the paid-attention spotlight, and the explicit-identity batch refresh. v4 (stage S3.5) is the first revision that REMOVES rows. The 12 public-API tools were retired whole and alias-free (owner decision D-DS2), so 26 rows lost their subject. They were handled in three ways, never left dangling. RETARGETED, because the user intent survives on a new owner: the known-pool-address rows to the single-pair snapshot, the many-known-identities rows to the batch refresh, the profile and boost feed rows to the spotlight document, and the narrative drill-down rows to the narrative aggregate that now yields the metaIds the screening boards take. REMOVED, because plan 4.6 records them as named omissions (owner decision D-DS3) and no tool answers them: the community-takeover feed, the per-token promotional-order ledger, and the ad-placement feed (paid ads survive only as an `onlyAds` FILTER on the screening boards, which is not a feed anyone can ask for). ADDED: rows for the three tools S3.5 landed on reclaimed identities, phrased around the capabilities that are actually new on them - server-side chain scoping on search, deepest-of-returned-window routing on the token pool list, and per-chain aggregates on narratives - because a reclaimed toolId whose rows only describe the retired behaviour would prove nothing about the tool that now holds it. v5 (stage S4) adds the deep-dive family: `pair.details`, `candles`, `trades` and `top.traders`. These are the namespace's first contract-level and wallet-level tools, so none of their rows are retargeted from a retired subject - every one is new intent that no DexScreener tool could answer before. Each tool carries at least one blind row and one protocol-aware row, plus one multi-tool row for the safety-then-chart-then-flow sequence the plan's section 5 describes, which is the sequence the four tools exist to make possible in one namespace.",
